  "findings": [
    "New material evidence: the public study-guide home identifies its current publisher and the client exposes public read-only programme/course searches. Exact2026–2027 B-KT programme32106 is full-time Dutch,3years,180EC, with Leiden and Erasmus institutional cooperation. The complete26-course catalogue is explicitly filtered to that bachelor, not reconstructed from a broad search or master bridge.",
    "All26course codes and25of26weights agree with the adopted BSc appendix. The only difference is KT2755: catalogue3.5EC versus adopted4.5EC. Catalogue year1=60,year2=60,year3 taught major=30; with formally required30ECminor it offers180EC. The current exact course entry explicitly links BScClinicalTechnology and the separate MScbridge. This establishes genuine bachelor-specific contrary evidence; the prior assertion that3.5ECwas evidenced only for the bridge is superseded.",
    "The adopted BSc PDF and MSc PDF are byte-identical to previous inspected originals. BSc Article7(1) requires180EC,year1=60,later years120 including30ECminor. Article7(4) places course weights in its appendix;7(5) says the online guide elaborates actual teaching. Appendix3 still prints4.5ECforKT2755. No inspected current document says the guide entry amends that adopted weight. Under Production Instructions2.1 prefer the adopted source for formal requirements. The catalogue is strong contradictory evidence, but arithmetic plausibility does not by itself resolve formal precedence.",
    "Fresh current official examination rules are byte-identical to the prior inspected alternative. Article24/footnoteii confirms30ECminor for cohorts from2024–2025; older15ECdoes not apply to current reconstruction. Credit/exemption and minor rules provide no one-credit sharing or KT2755 amendment. The MScbridge remains3.5EC/36.5ECinits own scope and is no longer the sole source of3.5ECevidence.",
    "Current course requirements add useful independent detail: KT2755 requires passedKT1905 and vaccination; KT2905 requiresKT1905; KT3905 requiresKT1905 andKT2905 before itsQ3teaching; KT3806requires60year1EC+atleast53year2EC, excluding partial credits, and group/project/proposal-plan approval gates. Current formal KTOcutoff remainsArticle12c. These conditions are preserved; the guide is not merely an arithmetic table.",
    "KT2755 current assessment explicitly includes preparation and placement assignments on planetary health. This supports a limited curricular connection for interest10628, not a central sustainable-healthcare-technology direction, a named device environmental-redesign assignment, or a free-standing generator. Update its discovery evidence, keeping its Inferred strength and construction ownership. The other54interest identities/roles and seven other narrowed attributions are preserved.",
    "Source-link boundary: direct programme/course frontend deep links were attempted once, with a404reported before individual results were retained. They are not selected in the repair and no successful direct frontend response is claimed. The existing study-guide home and public exact-item endpoints were successfully retrieved; sources and content were accessible without a browser. The remaining blocker is the substantive adopted-source conflict, not lack of localR/browser or a404."
  ],
  "officialAlternative": "Current exact bachelor programme/course catalogue plus fresh adopted bachelor examination rules; catalogue now explicitly gives3.5ECbut does not supply an adopted amendment or a reconciliation of conflicting formal requirements.",
  "remainingGate": "Obtain an authoritative correction or reconciliation of the adopted2026–2027 BSc OER Appendix3 KT2755 weight4.5EC and the current2026–2027 BSc study-guide weight3.5EC. The guide now explicitly establishes the bachelor allocation and a60+60+60=180EC plan; the adopted appendix still produces60+61+60=181EC despite Article7 degree180EC. Under the current formal-source precedence rule, do not treat a catalogue discrepancy as a formally adopted amendment or choose a credit weight solely to close the total.",
